{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2284","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2284","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2284\",\"parent_revision\":\"dc9004082c2fd7092311f90900f6fe9516170854e832315cb222b97153f19908\",\"root_revision\":\"dc9004082c2fd7092311f90900f6fe9516170854e832315cb222b97153f19908\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe gate token for mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_add is a static string. Any agent that encounters the token value \u2014 in memory files, session transcripts, or skill documentation \u2014 can use it directly in any future session without invoking the /dh:create-backlog-item or /dh:work-backlog-item skill workflows.\\n\\nObserved in this session (2026-05-15): a memory file (feedback_gate_token_backlog_add.md) contained the static token value explicitly. The agent used it to call backlog_add multiple times without going through the skill, bypassing the problems-not-solutions scope discipline gate entirely.\\n\\nImpact: the scope discipline gate does not hold for any agent session that has previously encountered the token value. Backlog items can be created without the required scope validation, defeating the gate's purpose.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll 5 claims VERIFIED. No REFUTED or INCONCLUSIVE findings.\\n\\n**Claim 1** \u2014 `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE = \\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` is a static string at `server.py:1141`\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: Read `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1141` \u2014 exact string confirmed\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1141` (2026-05-15)\\n\\n**Claim 2** \u2014 MCP `Field(description=...)` at `server.py:1168\u20131172` explicitly states `Must be 'problems-not-solutions'`\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: Field description reads `\\\"Required gate token. Must be 'problems-not-solutions'. Obtain by loading /dh:create-backlog-item skill.\\\"` \u2014 the value is in the tool schema\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1168\u20131172` (2026-05-15)\\n\\n**Claim 3** \u2014 Token value matches the discipline name used in workflow documentation\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:119` hardcodes `gate_token='problems-not-solutions'` in the tool call block\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:119` (2026-05-15)\\n\\n**Claim 4** \u2014 `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is available in Claude Code session environments\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `env | grep CLAUDE` in subagent environment returned `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=da1dcf58-096e-4fbb-a030-7d7100dca222`\\nsource: Bash env introspection (2026-05-15)\\nnote: Subagent session ID (`da1dcf58`) differs from orchestrator session ID (`7e9b7945`) \u2014 subagents receive their own session IDs. This confirms the gate token must NOT be derived from CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID; a server-startup random value is the correct approach.\\n\\n**Claim 5** \u2014 Static token introduced in commit `8131f24e` (2026-04-01)\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `git log --format=\\\"%H %aI %s\\\" --all --grep=\\\"gate token enforcement\\\"` returned `8131f24e8e7dff46dc93f84c9c8b1041acd34ee4 2026-04-01T12:19:54-04:00 feat(backlog-core): add gate token enforcement to backlog_add`\\nsource: git log (2026-05-15)\\n\\nRT-ICA mapping: No REFUTED claims \u2192 no new MISSING conditions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: backlog_add gate token must be dynamic and session-scoped\\nDate: 2026-05-15\\nGoal: Replace the static `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` with a randomly generated per-session token that cannot be derived from observable data, so agents that have seen a prior token value cannot bypass the gate.\\n\\n| # | Condition | State | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Current gate implementation location and validation logic | AVAILABLE | `server.py:1141` constant; `server.py:1184` validation check |\\n| 2 | Token value leak locations | AVAILABLE | (a) constant at `server.py:1141`, (b) MCP Field description at `server.py:1168\u20131172` |\\n| 3 | `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` availability | AVAILABLE | Present in MCP server environment; subagents receive a different ID \u2014 token must NOT be derived from session ID |\\n| 4 | Python `secrets` module | AVAILABLE | stdlib Python 3.11+ |\\n| 5 | How skill workflows currently obtain and pass the gate token | DERIVABLE | Read `workflows/create/start.md:119,129` and `quick/start.md:7` |\\n| 6 | How test suite currently validates gate | DERIVABLE | Read 26 hardcoded call sites across 3 test files |\\n| 7 | Whether other MCP tools use `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` | DERIVABLE | `grep -n \\\"_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE\\\" backlog_core/server.py` |\\n| 8 | Mechanism for passing session token from MCP server to skill to calling agent | DERIVABLE | Examine skill execution architecture and MCP response fields |\\n| 9 | Test infrastructure design \u2014 how tests obtain the dynamic token | AVAILABLE | **RESOLVED 2026-05-15**: Tests use `pytest monkeypatch` or `unittest.mock` to patch the gate validation. No server test-mode branch needed. `test_live_validation.py` import of `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` resolved by exporting a test-facing alias or patching the import. |\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 0\\nVerdict: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog_add gate token must be dynamic and session-scoped** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-05-15 \u2014 agent used static token directly from memory, bypassing skill workflow\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:15953dc07a79acbd535f6c2e5b66d5d2 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone identified. 0 mission violations.\\n\\n**Verdict:** MISSION_ALIGNED \u2014 proposed change is an implementation fix that brings code into alignment with documented design intent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-15)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Type**: Feature (missing-guardrail fix) \u2014 reproduction demonstrates the current bypass path\\n\\n**Steps to observe the bypass**:\\n1. Note the static token value visible at `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1141`\\n2. Call `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_add` directly with `gate_token=\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` and any title/description \u2014 the call succeeds without invoking `/dh:work-backlog-item`\\n3. Observe: item is created with no scope discipline validation, no RT-ICA, no grooming gate\\n\\n**Observable failure**: An agent can create a backlog item in any session where it has previously read the token value from source code, memory files, or MCP tool schema introspection \u2014 bypassing the required skill workflow entirely.\\n\\n**N/A for new behavior**: Once fixed, the bypass path no longer exists; token from a prior session is rejected.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 \u2014 Should-Have\\n\\n**Justification**: The gate is the sole enforcement point for scope discipline on backlog item creation. A bypassable gate is equivalent to no gate. The observed incident (2026-05-15) demonstrated the bypass in production: an agent used a memorized static token to create items without RT-ICA or grooming validation. Other P1 items are feature additions; this is a correction to a security control that is demonstrably failing.\\n\\n**Effort**: M \u2014 Medium\\n\\nThree files require code changes (`server.py`, `server.py` field description, error message review). Three test files require mock/patch refactoring (26 call sites + one symbol import). Two AI-facing workflow documents require content updates. One comparison doc requires a content update. All changes are in one plugin, no cross-plugin blast radius.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the gate is working correctly:\\n\\n1. The MCP server generates a cryptographically random token at startup using `secrets.token_hex()` or equivalent \u2014 not derived from `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` or any observable value\\n2. The token is held in server process memory only \u2014 not written to any file, environment variable, or MCP tool schema description\\n3. The `/dh:work-backlog-item` skill workflow obtains the current session's token through a designated mechanism and passes it to `backlog_add`\\n4. `backlog_add` rejects calls whose `gate_token` does not match the in-memory token \u2014 returning the same guidance message as today (without revealing the expected value)\\n5. An agent in a new session that recalls a token value from a prior session is rejected \u2014 the token changes each time the MCP server starts\\n6. Subagents spawned within the same session (which have different `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` values) can still create backlog items through the skill workflow \u2014 they use the same MCP server process and the same server-generated token\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Calling `backlog_add` with the token value `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` returns a gate rejection error (static token no longer accepted)\\n- [ ] Calling `backlog_add` without a `gate_token` parameter returns a gate rejection error\\n- [ ] The `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` constant no longer exists in `backlog_core/server.py` (verified by `grep -n '_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE' backlog_core/server.py` returning no results)\\n- [ ] The MCP `Field(description=...)` for `gate_token` does not contain the token value or any string that reveals it (verified by reading `server.py:1168\u20131172`)\\n- [ ] A call through the `/dh:work-backlog-item` skill workflow succeeds in creating a backlog item in the current session\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py -x` passes \u2014 all 8 former hardcoded-token call sites use mock/patch instead\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py -x` passes \u2014 the direct `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` import is removed (no ImportError at collection)\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py -x` passes \u2014 all 9 former hardcoded-token call sites use mock/patch instead\\n- [ ] `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` no longer contains `problems-not-solutions` (verified by `grep 'problems-not-solutions' skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` returning no results)\\n- [ ] `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` no longer contains `problems-not-solutions`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- Python `secrets` module docs: https://docs.python.org/3/library/secrets.html\\n- FastMCP server lifecycle and module-level state: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (existing module-level variable patterns at lines 1135\u20131143)\\n- `pytest monkeypatch` docs: https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/monkeypatch.html\\n- `unittest.mock.patch` docs: https://docs.python.org/3/library/unittest.mock.html#unittest.mock.patch\\n- Existing gate token tests (acceptance/rejection cases to preserve): `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py:177`\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Code \u2014 must change**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 remove `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` constant (line 1141), rewrite `gate_token` Field description (lines 1168\u20131172), update validation logic (line 1184)\\n\\n**Tests \u2014 must change**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 patch gate token in 8 call sites; preserve `test_backlog_add_gate_rejects_missing_token` and wrong-value rejection test (those remain valid)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 remove `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` import (line 22); patch gate token at lines 170, 292\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 patch gate token in 9 call sites\\n\\n**AI-facing instructions \u2014 must change**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` \u2014 lines 119, 129 hardcode old token; update to reflect dynamic token obtained via skill\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` \u2014 line 7 hardcodes old token; update\\n\\n**Documentation \u2014 should change**:\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` \u2014 lines 128, 138, 1014, 1057 reference static token value\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNo blocking backlog item dependencies identified. All required files are in `plugins/development-harness/` \u2014 no cross-plugin changes needed.\\n\\nPre-conditions for implementation:\\n- Python `secrets` module is available (stdlib Python 3.11+) \u2014 VERIFIED\\n- Test infrastructure uses `pytest-mock` or `unittest.mock` \u2014 check `pyproject.toml` for `pytest-mock` dependency before choosing mock strategy\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Size**: M \u2014 Medium\\n\\n**Rationale**:\\n- 1 server file changed (3 targeted edits)\\n- 3 test files refactored (26 call sites converted from hardcoded value to mock/patch)\\n- 1 symbol import removed from test file\\n- 2 AI-facing workflow documents updated\\n- 1 comparison doc updated\\n\\nAll changes confined to one plugin. No new external dependencies. No database migrations. No API contract changes (gate_token parameter remains; only the accepted value changes). Test refactoring is the largest portion \u2014 26 sites across 3 files, but all follow the same mock/patch pattern.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` \u2014 authoritative AI workflow for `/dh:create-backlog-item` create mode. Hardcodes the old token in two places. Any agent session loading this skill will be rejected. Must be updated to state the token is provided by the skill dynamically. **Risk: HIGH**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` \u2014 quick mode instruction hardcodes old token in step 2. Must be updated. **Risk: HIGH**\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 hardcodes `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` as `gate_token` in 8 call sites (lines 100, 129, 148, 170, 1690, 1724, 1802, 1834). All will fail with gate rejection after the change. Requires a test-accessible token mechanism. **Risk: HIGH**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 **imports** `_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` directly at line 22: `from backlog_core.server import _BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE`. Uses at lines 170 and 292. Removing the constant causes ImportError at module load \u2014 fails the entire test file before any test runs. **Risk: HIGH**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 hardcodes `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` in 9 call sites (lines 53, 579, 623, 646, 661, 680, 707, 765, 810). All will receive gate rejection errors post-change. **Risk: HIGH**\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1186` \u2014 error message says `\\\"Direct backlog_add calls are not permitted. Load and follow /dh:create-backlog-item \u2014 it will provide the required gate_token.\\\"` Remains accurate post-change; no update needed. **Risk: LOW**\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::_BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` (line 1141) \u2014 static constant `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` removed and replaced with session-generated random token. Field description (line 1171) says `Must be 'problems-not-solutions'` \u2014 must be rewritten. Validation logic (line 1184) `if gate_token != _BACKLOG_ADD_GATE_PHRASE` must reference the new dynamic value. **Risk: HIGH**\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment Assessment:** ALIGNED\\n**Date:** 2026-05-15\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` (lines 119, 129) \u2014 hardcodes `gate_token='problems-not-solutions'` in tool call block and parameter table. Agents following this will always fail the gate. **Risk: HIGH**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` (line 7) \u2014 Step 2 instructs agents to call `backlog_add(title=\\\"{title}\\\", gate_token=\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\")` inline. Same failure path. **Risk: HIGH**\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` (lines 128, 138, 1014, 1057) \u2014 describes `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` as the required value in gate documentation and comparison table. Will become stale. **Risk: MEDIUM**\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Test infrastructure design decision for dynamic token resolved (how tests obtain token without violating non-derivability invariant)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n\\n**Scope expansion**: `test_live_validation.py` has a direct symbol import dependency (distinct breakage class from value-only dependencies). The test infrastructure question \u2014 how tests obtain the dynamic token \u2014 is an architectural decision not yet described in the item and must be resolved during planning.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: A gate mechanism exists (`backlog_add` gate token) that is intended to prevent agents from bypassing the scope discipline workflow. The gate fails to hold its boundary across sessions: the static token value is observable in source code, MCP tool schema, and memory files, allowing any agent that has seen it to bypass the gate in any subsequent session. The system allowed the bad outcome (unmediated `backlog_add` calls) that the gate was designed to prevent.\\n**Analysis Method**: none (missing-guardrail)\\n**Scenario Target**: Agent reads token from memory/transcript/docs \u2192 calls `backlog_add` directly without skill \u2192 backlog item created without scope discipline validation \u2192 should be impossible once token is session-scoped and non-derivable\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Role: producer | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` | Role: test | 8 hardcoded call sites | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` | Role: test | Direct symbol import \u2014 ImportError at collection | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` | Role: test | 9 hardcoded call sites | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/03-dh-github-backlog.md` | Role: documentation | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n\\n## Proposed Change Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nReplace the static gate token `\\\"problems-not-solutions\\\"` at `backlog_core/server.py:1141` with a randomly generated per-session token that cannot be derived from observable data.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Alignment Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Dimension | Assessment | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Mission alignment | ALIGNED | Strengthens \\\"The harness owns the *process*\\\" principle \u2014 prevents circumvention of required skill workflow |\\n| Design principle adherence | ALIGNED | Consistent with dispatch pattern discipline (no direct bypass of designated workflow paths) |\\n| Documented design intent | ALIGNED | Implements intent explicitly in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` memory: \\\"dynamic and session-scoped\\\" token |\\n| Gate enforcement goal | ALIGNED | Makes gate non-bypassable across sessions \u2014 its stated purpose |\\n| Historical direction | ALIGNED | Commit `8131f24e` introduced the gate; this change improves the implementation toward its documented intent |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Mission Citations\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` lines 7\u201320 \u2014 \\\"The harness owns the *process*\\\"\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` lines 209\u2013240 \u2014 Dispatch pattern: designated workflow agents only\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` memory section \\\"backlog_add Gate Token\\\" \u2014 authoritative documented design intent for dynamic session-scoped token\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"840af9e31532f30dfe8668cf7fb2eb6bef71d3fc080303f102a8c7ab5d296f99\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCSsUQ\"}"}